_:b0_r10b1 crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "Evidence archive: public postings of Metaconceptual Art (2011-2012)";
    crm:P2_has_type aat:300404670;
    crm:P72_has_language aat:300388277;
    a crm:E33_E41_Linguistic_Appellation.
_:b0_r10b2 crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "record:evidence-pastebin-2011-2012";
    crm:P2_has_type aat:300312355;
    a crm:E42_Identifier.
_:b0_r10b3 crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "Evidence status: publicly verifiable on a third-party platform, and the earliest such evidence in this collection. The postings are readable by anyone at https://pastebin.com/AmQ3P87v and https://pastebin.com/18ndp2CF ; both are set never to expire. Their dates are assigned by the platform at the moment of posting and are carried in the page markup as 'Thursday 22nd of November 2012 11:19:57 PM CDT' and 'Monday 28th of November 2011 07:51:51 AM CDT'. Unlike a profile biography, the body of a paste is fixed once posted. The platform also records public circulation: 950 views for the 2012 posting and 433 for the 2011 one at the time of compilation. Nothing here is studio-held, so verification requires no access to the private archive.";
    crm:P2_has_type aat:300435416;
    a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object.
_:b0_r10b4 crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "Relation to the published Eight Sentences. The 2012 posting is the earliest located instance of the sentence sequence and predates its publication on this site by fourteen years. Its wording is the wording published here, allowing for three trivial variances: 'commodification of Art, and its relationship' has since lost its comma, 'the Art World , and Art History' has lost a space, and 'Transcendance' has been corrected to 'Transcendence'. The persistence of a misspelling across the interval, and its later silent normalisation, are recorded because they are the sort of detail by which a text's descent is traced. The sequence's stated debt to Sol LeWitt's 'Sentences on Conceptual Art' is not present in the 2012 posting and appears to be a later framing.";
    crm:P2_has_type aat:300435416;
    a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object.
_:b0_r10b5 crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "Limits. Both postings are the artist's own; the platform dates when he said something publicly, not whether what he said was true. They therefore evidence the public existence of the term and its definition at those dates, and nothing about the 2009 auction, which neither posting mentions. The 2011 posting describes its poem as written 'a few years ago', which would place composition somewhere in the late 2000s; that is the artist's own statement, made in 2011 rather than in retrospect from the present, and it narrows but does not close the gap to the asserted 2007 origin. The origin date itself remains unevidenced. Both postings link to a Sun & Rain Works page on Facebook. That page has since been deleted by the studio, and the Internet Archive holds no capture of it, so it cannot be examined and any earlier material it carried is lost. Its former existence is not in doubt: the 2012 posting cites its address and presents the eight characteristics as the page's content, which places the definition on that page on or before 2012-11-22. The postings recorded here are consequently the surviving witness to a source that no longer exists, and they are load-bearing for that reason.";
    crm:P2_has_type aat:300435416;
    a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object.
_:b0_r10b6 crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "Preservation note. Of the sources that once carried this material, several no longer exist: the Facebook page has been deleted, the YouTube videos cited in the 2013 correspondence are gone, and the mailbox from which that correspondence was sent has been closed. What survives does so on a third-party platform the studio does not control, in two postings set never to expire. Their continued availability is not guaranteed by anyone. The studio has therefore taken a local copy of both postings - the paste bodies and the rendered pages, the latter retained because they carry the platform's own timestamp string that the raw endpoint omits - published alongside this record with checksums at data/evidence/pastebin-2011-2012/. Those files are a preservation copy and not the dated source: a local file proves what was retrieved and when it was retrieved, and nothing more. The dating rests on Pastebin's records, which assign a posting timestamp the poster cannot alter, and should be verified against the live URLs for as long as they resolve.";
    crm:P2_has_type aat:300435416;
    a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object.
_:b0_r10b7 crm:P14_carried_out_by mca:sun-and-rain-works;
    crm:P4_has_time-span _:b0_r10b8;
    a crm:E65_Creation;
    rdfs:label "Compilation of the 2011-2012 public-posting evidence record".
_:b0_r10b8 crm:P82a_begin_of_the_begin "2026-01-01T00:00:00Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime>;
    crm:P82b_end_of_the_end "2026-12-31T23:59:59Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime>;
